---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { fullSrc, IMAGES } from '../../lib/site';
import Pic from '../../components/Pic.astro';
import MotionClips from '../../components/MotionClips.astro';
import DataFlowDiagram from '../../components/DataFlowDiagram.astro';
import DaySequence from '../../components/DaySequence.astro';
import { stats, modules, stack, broke, differently, screenshots, shot } from '../../data/internal-dashboard';
---
<Base title="Case study: the Internal Dashboard" section="ai"
  description="How Cameron Kuey took Doodle Pirates Foundation’s all-in-one Internal Dashboard from concept to production in under two weeks with Claude Code and AI coding agents: 152 reviewed PRs, 1,218 tests.">
  <article>
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="page-head wide">
        <ol class="crumbs eyebrow" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><li><a href="/ai-builds">AI Builds</a></li><li>Case study</li></ol>
        <h1>An all-in-one Internal Dashboard, <em>concept to production in under two weeks.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">As product owner at Doodle Pirates Foundation, I designed and shipped one role-based platform for the whole team, built with Claude Code, Claude Design and AI coding agents, with a human reviewing every change.</p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <section style="padding-top:16px"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="case cs-hero">
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p>
          <div class="stats" style="margin-top:20px">
            {stats.map((s) => <div class="stat"><b>{s.value}</b><span>{s.label}</span></div>)}
          </div>
          <p>Role: product owner. Doodle Pirates Foundation · Director of Business Operations.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="cs-shot">
          <span class="tag">Sample data</span>
          <Pic id={shot.myWork.id} alt={shot.myWork.alt} eager sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 640px" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
      <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>The problem</h2></div>
      <div class="prose block-text">
        <p>Doodle Pirates Foundation is a nonprofit, and much of the team is neurodivergent. I built the dashboard partly to give each person one simple place that shows what to focus on each day.</p>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
      <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>What it does</h2></div>
      <div class="prose block-text">
        <p>One role-based platform that unifies:</p>
        <ul class="taglist">{modules.map((m) => <li>{m}</li>)}</ul>
        <p>By my estimate, it avoids <strong>$1,000+ per employee in annual software costs</strong>.</p>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
      <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>Ask Otis</h2></div>
      <div class="prose block-text">
        <p>Ask Otis is a Claude-powered assistant built into the dashboard. Ask it to add a task, update one, or change a project or milestone, and it comes back with an editable card. Nothing changes until the person presses Approve, and the server checks their permissions again before saving.</p>
        <h2>From meetings to daily focus</h2>
        <p>The dashboard doesn’t read meeting notes. Action items from meetings go into the task list, added by people and by AI assistants we run outside the dashboard.</p>
        <p>Every weekday at 6:30 AM, the dashboard picks 3 to 5 tasks for each person’s daily focus, using AI with a short reason for each. If the AI is slow or down, a rule-based picker fills in, so no one starts the day without a list. By my estimate, going from meeting action items to a daily focus this way saves about 5 hours a week.</p>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
      <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>How it was built</h2></div>
      <div>
        <div class="prose block-text"><p>I directed AI coding agents as product owner and reviewed their work: 152 pull requests, each one reviewed, backed by 1,218 automated tests.</p></div>
        <dl class="spec">
          {stack.map(([k, v]) => <div><dt>{k}</dt><dd>{v}</dd></div>)}
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>How data flows</h2></div>
        <div class="prose block-text"><p>Everyone signs in with their work Google account. The front end and API run together on one Cloudflare Worker. Every write goes through the API, which checks permissions and then writes to Airtable, the source of truth. Docs are real Google Docs. Shifts, PTO and sick days go one way to Google Calendar, and nothing is read back from those events. Ask Otis only suggests; a person approves before anything is saved.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:32px"><DataFlowDiagram /></div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>A day in the dashboard</h2></div>
        <div class="prose block-text"><p>A typical day for someone on the team, from meeting action items to a confirmed week.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:40px"><DaySequence /></div>
    </div></section>

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>See it in motion</h2></div>
        <div class="prose block-text"><p>Short screen recordings from the dashboard’s sample-data mode.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:40px"><MotionClips /></div>
    </div></section>

    {broke.length > 0 && (
      <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>What broke &amp; how I fixed it</h2></div>
        <ol class="numbered">{broke.map((b) => <li><b>{b.title}</b><p>{b.fix}</p></li>)}</ol>
      </div></section>
    )}
    {differently.length > 0 && (
      <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap cs-grid">
        <div class="sec-head cs-label"><h2>What I’d do differently</h2></div>
        <ol class="numbered">{differently.map((d) => <li><p>{d}</p></li>)}</ol>
      </div></section>
    )}

    <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2>Screens</h2><p class="eyebrow">Sample data only</p></div>
      <div class="shots dash-shots" data-gallery>
        {screenshots.map((s) => (
          <figure class={`shot${s.phone ? ' is-phone' : ''}`}>
            <a class="shot-img" href={fullSrc(s.id)} data-lb data-w={IMAGES[s.id].w} data-h={IMAGES[s.id].h} data-cap={`${s.label} (sample data)`} aria-label={`View larger: ${s.alt}`}>
              <span class="tag">Sample data</span>
              <Pic id={s.id} alt={s.alt} sizes={s.phone ? '(max-width: 900px) 50vw, 260px' : '(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 560px'} />
            </a>
            <figcaption><b>{s.label}</b>{s.note && <span>{s.note}</span>}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="caption" style="margin-top:20px">Every name, task and number on these screens is invented sample data. One vendor name in a sample task title is blurred. The dashboard and its code belong to Doodle Pirates Foundation and are private.</p>
      <div class="btns"><a class="btn solid" href="/ai-builds">More AI builds →</a><a class="btn" href="/contact">Ask me about it</a></div>
    </div></section>
  </article>
</Base>
